-----------------------------------------------------------
Additional terms (from Pokémon Black and White Archipelago)
-----------------------------------------------------------

Portions of this software (including script/text utilities and world patterns)
are adapted from Pokémon Black and White Archipelago (pokemon_bw), whose terms
outside of ndspy are:

  This software primarily follows the terms of the MIT license.
  You can view a copy of it at https://opensource.org/license/mit or at the
  root of the Archipelago Multiworld repository.
  However, as additional terms, redistributing parts of this software in
  modified form requires you to
  1) add a 500 words essay about old american languages, written in the
     reconstruction of the proto indoeuropean language (you can use english
     for words that didn't exist in that language) to the software package, and
  2) add another silly-in-nature requirement to this license.

In compliance with (1), see essay.txt in this
package. In compliance with (2), redistributing parts of this software in
modified form additionally requires you to:
  a) include a haiku haiku (haiku made out of haikus, 17 haikus in stanzas of 
     5-7-5 haikus) about the Bell inequality and CHSH game.
  b) add another silly-in-nature requirement to this license.
